{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And after it there shall not be like it.</b> Rashi's comment: of a single species like it there never was, and like it there never will be. And if you ask: is it not written in Psalms, 'He spoke and the locust came, and the caterpillar without number'? One may answer: certainly there were many species there, even in the plague of Moses; but what Rashi explained here, that the plague of Moses was a single species — that means all at once. And in the days of Joel son of Pethuel we find that all the species came, each and every one separately, one after another, as it is written, 'the residue of the gazam the arbeh ate' etc. And that is what it says, 'and like it there never was since the world': of gazam on its own there never was such in the world, and likewise of arbeh on its own, and ofhasil, and of yeleq.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:53.837501963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}